WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:05.530
YouTube has been caught despite all of its
claims that it's cleaning up its algorithm

00:00:05.530 --> 00:00:12.830
actively promoting videos containing completely
anti scientific climate change denial.

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:17.660
This is based on a new report from Avaaz,
which I'm going to tell you about in a second.

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:22.779
Many of you know that over the last 18 months,
our YouTube channel has been absolutely crushed

00:00:22.779 --> 00:00:27.420
by YouTube recommended video algorithm and
its monetization algorithm.

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:32.570
I'll have updated numbers for you from 2020
2019 in total later this week or early next

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:33.570
week.

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:38.030
I'm not going to retell the full details of
the story right now, but the gist of it is

00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:45.040
that in late 2018 YouTube started promoting
so-called authoritative content over fringe

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:47.780
content and we were wrapped up in that.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:53.610
What they've they've done effectively is recommend
corporate legacy YouTube channels like CNN,

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:58.630
MSNBC, and Fox news uses YouTube channels
over independent channels like ours, and it

00:00:58.630 --> 00:00:59.630
has hurt us hugely.

00:00:59.630 --> 00:01:05.600
I told you a couple of months ago that I believed
we were losing about two to 3 million views

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:12.259
per month since early 2019 but it turns out
that it's actually even worse than that.

00:01:12.259 --> 00:01:19.069
If you go back to February of 2017 we got
more than 6 million views just from YouTube

00:01:19.069 --> 00:01:20.259
recommendations.

00:01:20.259 --> 00:01:21.299
That's not our whole channel.

00:01:21.299 --> 00:01:23.539
That's just from the recommendations.

00:01:23.539 --> 00:01:31.329
In December of 2019 it was 600,000 that is
a literal decimation of our recommended views.

00:01:31.329 --> 00:01:36.909
The shortfall is as much as five and a half
million views in a month.

00:01:36.909 --> 00:01:38.919
This is destroying the channel.

00:01:38.919 --> 00:01:44.729
I truly, when I see those numbers, it's so
disheartening and crushing to see it.

00:01:44.729 --> 00:01:50.649
Given what we have done over the last several
years to be a bigger and bigger part of the

00:01:50.649 --> 00:01:58.219
discussion on YouTube and to see our recommendations
shrink to barely 10% of what they once were.

00:01:58.219 --> 00:02:05.899
And then we find out because of this report
that Avaaz puts out, they look up 5,000 videos

00:02:05.899 --> 00:02:12.000
which come up when you search terms, climate
change, global warming and related terms,

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:17.969
and then they look at 5,000 videos and then
they checked which videos is YouTube recommending

00:02:17.969 --> 00:02:20.260
when you are watching those videos, right?

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:24.540
If you search for climate change and watch
a video, what does YouTube then suggest that

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:29.370
you watch in the up next bar of videos that
shows up next to or below the video you're

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:33.519
watching, depending on whether you're on mobile
or on a computer, depending on which search

00:02:33.519 --> 00:02:40.120
term you used, anywhere from eight to 21%
of the videos that YouTube recommended you

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:41.120
watch.

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:46.459
Next included climate science denial of different
kinds.

00:02:46.459 --> 00:02:49.140
21% is more than one out of five.

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:54.939
Now if YouTube said, we're not taking any
position on promoting authoritative content

00:02:54.939 --> 00:03:01.069
over fringe, reliable content over conspiracies,
I'd say fine, they're not taking a position.

00:03:01.069 --> 00:03:05.829
Their algorithm is not trying to promote authoritative
over fringe content and there's some climate

00:03:05.829 --> 00:03:11.770
signs, denial stuff that has shown up, but
YouTube says we are going to promote authoritative

00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:19.719
stuff over fringe content and conspiracy content
and it costs our channel two, three, five

00:03:19.719 --> 00:03:22.240
and a half million views per month.

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:24.280
But supposedly it's worth it, right?

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:27.889
Because they're not promoting BS conspiracies
and fringe content.

00:03:27.889 --> 00:03:34.970
And yet in some cases, one out of five climate
change recommendations are for climate science

00:03:34.970 --> 00:03:37.269
